          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "气候 (qìhòu) is built from 气 'air' and 候 'a season', both inherited from Middle Chinese, khj+jH and huwH (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which glosses the second 'to wait on'; the sense of a season is not given there."
            }
          ]
        },
